1
00:03:49,655 --> 00:03:55,655
It was supposed to be the safest room in the house.

2
00:07:39,310 --> 00:07:45,310
Panic Room is a crime, drama, thriller film directed by David Fincher.

3
00:11:28,965 --> 00:11:34,965
Trapped in their New York brownstone's panic room, a hidden chamber built as a sanctuary in the event of break-ins, newly divorced Meg Altman and her
young daughter Sarah play a deadly game of cat-and-mouse with three intruders - Burnham, Raoul and Junior - during a brutal home invasion.

4
00:15:18,620 --> 00:15:24,620
But the room itself is the focal point because what
the intruders really want is inside it.

5
00:19:08,275 --> 00:19:14,275
Meg Altman, played by Jodie Foster.

6
00:22:57,931 --> 00:23:03,931
Sarah Altman, played by Kristen Stewart.

7
00:26:47,586 --> 00:26:53,586
Burnham, played by Forest Whitaker.

8
00:30:37,241 --> 00:30:43,241
Raoul, played by Dwight Yoakam.

9
00:34:26,896 --> 00:34:32,896
Junior, played by Jared Leto.

10
00:38:16,551 --> 00:38:22,551
Stephen Altman, played by Patrick Bauchau.

11
00:42:06,206 --> 00:42:12,206
Panic Room is a 2002 American thriller film directed by David Fincher.

12
00:45:55,862 --> 00:46:01,862
The film stars Jodie Foster and Kristen Stewart as a mother and daughter whose new home is
invaded by burglars, played by Forest Whitaker, Jared Leto, and Dwight Yoakam.

13
00:49:45,517 --> 00:49:51,517
The script was written by David Koepp, whose screenplay was
inspired by news coverage in 2000 about panic rooms.

14
00:53:35,172 --> 00:53:41,172
The film was Fincher's fifth feature film, following Fight Club (1999).

15
00:57:24,827 --> 00:57:30,827
Fincher and Koepp brought together a crew of people
with whom each had worked with before.

16
01:01:14,482 --> 01:01:20,482
The house and its panic room were built on a Raleigh Studios lot.

17
01:05:04,137 --> 01:05:10,137
Nicole Kidman was originally cast as the mother, but she
left after aggravating a previous injury.

18
01:08:53,793 --> 01:08:59,793
Her departure threatened the completion of the film,
but Foster quickly replaced Kidman.

19
01:12:43,448 --> 01:12:49,448
The filmmakers used computer-generated imagery to create the illusion
of the film camera moving through the house's rooms.

20
01:16:33,103 --> 01:16:39,103
Foster became pregnant during the shooting schedule, so
filming was suspended until after she gave birth.

21
01:20:22,758 --> 01:20:28,758
The film's production cost $48 million.

22
01:24:12,413 --> 01:24:18,413
The film was commercially released in the United States and
Canada on March 29, 2002 by Sony Pictures Releasing.

23
01:28:02,068 --> 01:28:08,068
The film grossed $30 million on its opening weekend.

24
01:31:51,724 --> 01:31:57,724
In the United States and Canada, it grossed $96.4 million.

25
01:35:41,379 --> 01:35:47,379
In other territories, it grossed $100.7 million for a
worldwide total of $197.1 million.

26
01:39:31,034 --> 01:39:37,034
The film was positively reviewed by critics, who commended
Fincher's direction and Foster's performance.

27
01:43:20,689 --> 01:43:26,689
The film explores themes of new york city, hostage, bravery, ex husband, safe.

28
01:47:10,344 --> 01:47:16,344
The tone is mind_bending and dark and emotional.
